{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "exMrY_6xoTahcTnBt",
			"description": "Autopistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cheap, mass-produced sidearm found across a billion hive worlds: gang muscle, PDF conscripts and Guard officers who don't rate a laspistol all carry one. Consistently portrayed in Guard and Arbites fiction as the low-status \"poor man's laspistol.\"\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers stub weapons directly, but they must stay proportional to the autogun anchor (7d pi) they're built alongside. GURPS's own real-world pistol-calibre baseline sits at roughly the same fraction of the autogun the earlier pass used (avg 9/avg 18.5 = 49% pre-rescale), so the autopistol is rescaled by the same ratio the autogun itself moved (5d+1→7d, avg 18.5→24.5, ×1.32): 2d+2 pi (avg 9) becomes 3d+2 pi (avg 12.5), keeping full pi wounding for a modern jacketed round rather than the crude ball ammo an earlier pass assumed. Against flak (DR 30, raised twice since this line was first derived) it now penetrates 0% of hits — the autopistol has been pushed from \"a real but unimpressive threat\" to no threat at all against military-issue flak under the current armour anchors, leaving it relevant only against unarmoured targets; a GM wanting it to still matter against flak specifically would need to depart from this pistol-family scaling, which this entry does not do on its own authority. The Manstopper usage keeps the same pi+/divisor(0.5) shape and the same +1 die/+1 over the ball round relationship (3d+3(0.5) pi+, avg 13.5): it never penetrates flak or better (0% of hits, effective DR doubled by the divisor) but hits unarmoured flesh harder, the standard GURPS way to model an expanding round — more damage to flesh, worse against any DR. Handling: weight (2 lb) and min ST (7) are unchanged - GURPS's own pistol-weight convention (roughly ST 7 for a service-calibre autoloader this size) already applies here rather than the shoulder-arm sqrt formula, which this project reserves for rifles and heavier weapons. Bulk -2 and Rcl 2 are ordinary pistol figures.",
