		{
			"id": "eGE58NvXGebFKBY9S",
			"description": "Stub Revolver",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A well-made, reliable break-top or swing-cylinder handgun favoured by Inquisitorial acolytes, enforcers and anyone who prizes reliability over firepower or rate of fire; FFG-line background (used here only for relative calibration, per framework.md's source order) singles the stub revolver out as the higher-quality, slower-firing counterpart to the stub automatic.\n\nDesign: Single-action cycling caps RoF at 1 — there's no autofire mechanism. A heavier, hand-loaded magnum-class round (GURPS real-world baseline: a .44 Magnum runs about 3d pi, rescaled by the same ×1.32 ratio the autogun itself moved to 4d pi, avg 14) sits above the autopistol's 3d+2 pi (avg 12.5), reflecting a larger-calibre, better-machined round fired from a tighter, hand-fitted barrel — and stays well under the autogun's 7d pi rifle round. Average roll 14 penetrates flak (DR 30) on 0% of hits (worse than the autopistol's own 0% only in that neither now threatens flak at all) and never beats carapace (DR 70: 0%); like every stub pistol-calibre round in this file, the twice-raised flak anchor has pushed it below the threshold where it threatens military-grade armour, leaving it a threat to unarmoured targets only. Low Rcl (1) follows from GURPS convention for a heavier, well-balanced revolver.",
