		{
			"id": "elmowmV1PexTMlHay",
			"description": "Combat Shotgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A full-auto-capable military scattergun issued to void-ship boarding parties, PDF close-quarters units and Adeptus Arbites riot squads. \"Executioner\" shells are referenced in FFG-line background (relative calibration only, per framework.md) as a specialist close-range, armour-beating round issued to elite units rather than line troops.\n\nDesign: Buckshot and slug follow the usual GURPS shotgun split — short-ranged and hard-hitting versus long-ranged and precise — but are given single flat damage figures rather than the Basic Set's full range-banded pellet-spread rules, a deliberate simplification noted here for transparency. Both are rescaled by the same ×1.32 ratio the autogun itself moved: buckshot (4d+2 pi+, avg 16) becomes 6d pi+ (avg 21) and penetrates flak (DR 30) on just 1.0% of hits at point-blank range - the twice-raised flak anchor now stops a shotgun blast almost completely, matching a scattergun's real-world reputation against rigid plate even at the \"vest\" tier; slug (6d pi+, avg 21) becomes 8d pi+ (avg 28) and still can't beat carapace (DR 70: 0% of hits). The Executioner shell keeps the buckshot's short range but adds an armour divisor of (2) and is rescaled to track the lasgun exactly (7d(2) pi+, avg 24.5, per this entry's original design intent of \"the same figure as a standard lasgun\"): 0.6% against carapace (DR 70, effective 35), the same figure as the current lasgun. Handling: RoF is now per-mode rather than one blanket \"3\" copied across every ammunition type: buckshot keeps RoF 3 (a genuinely full-auto-capable close-range load, matching the lore's \"full-auto- capable military scattergun\"), while slug and the rare Executioner shell drop to RoF 1 - both are precision, longer-ranged or armour-beating rounds a gunner fires deliberately, one at a time, not sprayed on full auto, and neither pattern's lore ever shows it used that way.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Arbites"
			],
