		{
			"id": "efE2RLOO5MyRv0uWf",
			"description": "Pump Shotgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A civilian and militia pump-action scattergun common on agri and feral worlds and among hive gangers — a step down from the military combat shotgun, and the more commonly depicted shotgun among non-military characters in Imperial fiction.\n\nDesign: Same buckshot/slug split as the Combat Shotgun, toned down roughly half a die (matching the Combat Shotgun's own new figures) and locked to RoF 1 (manual pump cycling, no autofire) to reflect civilian manufacture rather than a military select-fire action: buckshot (avg 18.5) penetrates flak (DR 30) on 0% of hits at point-blank range - civilian buckshot no longer threatens military flak at all under the current anchors - and slug (avg 25.5) still fails against carapace (DR 70: 0% of hits). Handling: RoF 1 for both modes is unchanged and correct as-is - a pump-action shotgun has no autofire mechanism regardless of the load, so unlike the Combat Shotgun above there was never a per-mode RoF inconsistency to fix here. Weight, min ST, Bulk and Rcl are unchanged.",
