		{
			"id": "eCBBOcoit4P8Su45p",
			"description": "Hunting Rifle",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A bolt-action precision rifle common on agri, feral and frontier worlds, pressed into service as a stopgap sniper weapon by Guard marksmen and PDF units where a long-las isn't issued.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a realistic TL7 bolt-action big-game rifle (a real-world analogue, not a renamed catalogue item), rescaled by the same ×1.32 ratio the autogun itself moved (7d pi, avg 24.5, becomes 9d+1 pi, avg 32.5): a large single round for maximum penetration, RoF 1 for manual bolt cycling between shots. Kept below the long-las (8d(2) burn) in practical terms — full pi wounding and no armour divisor mean it's comparably lethal to an unarmoured target (65.0% through flak, DR 30) but does nothing against carapace-or-better armour (0% of hits at DR 70), in contrast to the long-las which at least keeps pace with a standard lasgun there. Handling: min ST corrected to 11 (√(10×9)≈9.5, bumped for a stiff- recoiling big-game round rather than a light sporting rifle - real hunting rifles chambered for genuinely large game run ST 10-11 in GURPS convention). Bulk -6 and Rcl 2 are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
